^SAMPLE = GSM5702566
!Sample_title = WT TIG 1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM5702566
!Sample_status = Public on Jun 09 2022
!Sample_submission_date = Nov 24 2021
!Sample_last_update_date = Jun 09 2022
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = colorectal adenocarcinoma (DLD1)
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: Wild Type
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: Tigecycline 10uM for 24h
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Tigecycline was dissolved in DMSO to 10mM. 1µl of this was added to 10ml of culture media to a final concentration of 10 µM. 1µl of DMSO was added to 10 ml of culture media in the control group. After 24h cells were collected for RNA extraction.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Cells were cultured at 37ºC in a humidified air atmosphere with 5% CO2. Cells were grown using high glucose Dulbecco’s Modified Eagle’s Medium (DMEM; Sigma, D5796) supplemented with 10% Fetal Bovine Serum (FBS) and 1% penicillin/streptomycin.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Total RNA was extracted from cell pellets using the Agilent Absolutely RNA Miniprep Kit following the manufacturer’s instructions
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Total RNA samples, 250ng with RQS=10 in a labchip analysis, were processed into cDNA sequencing libraries with the "QuantSeq 3‘ mRNA-Seq Library Prep Kit (FWD) for Illumina" (Lexogen, Cat.No. 015). Briefly, library generation is initiated by reverse transcription with oligodT priming, followed by a random-primed second strand synthesis. Primers from both steps contain Illumina-compatible sequences. Libraries were completed by PCR, and sequenced on an Illumina instrument (see below) by following manufacturer's protocols.  {This library preparation kit generates directional libraries stranded in the sense orientation (the read1 (the only read in single read format) has the sense orientation (--library-type fr-secondstrand in TopHat, --stranded=yes in HTSeq)}
!Sample_data_processing = Raw images generated by the sequencer are submitted to analysis, per-cycle basecalling and quality score assignment with Illumina's RTA (Real Time Analysis) integrated primary analysis software. Conversion of BCL (base calls) binary files to FASTQ format is subsequently performed with Local Run Manager GenerateFASTQ Analysis Module (Illumina).
!Sample_data_processing = Sequencing read alignment and quantification and differential gene expression analysis was performed in the Bluebee Genomics Platform, a cloud-based service provider (www.bluebee.com.)
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were first trimmed with bbduk from BBTools (Bushnell B., BBMap, https://sourceforge.net/projects/bbmap/) to remove adapter sequences and polyA tails.  Trimmed reads were aligned with STAR v 2.5 (Dobin A et al. Bioinformatics 29:15, 2013.) Read counting was performed with HTSeq (Anders S et al. Bioinformatics 31:166, 2015.)
!Sample_data_processing = Differential gene expression analysis was performed with DESeq2 (Love MI et al. Genome Biol 15:550, 2014)
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCh38/hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Normalized counts and result table from results() function, both from DESeq2.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL21697
!Sample_contact_name = Orlando,,Domínguez
!Sample_contact_email = genomica@cnio.es
!Sample_contact_laboratory = Genomics Core
!Sample_contact_institute = CNIO
!Sample_contact_address = Melchor F. Almagro 3
!Sample_contact_city = Madrid
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 28029
!Sample_contact_country = Spain
!Sample_instrument_model = NextSeq 550
!Sample_library_selection = cDNA
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic
!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN23425223
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX13218094
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE
!Sample_series_id = GSE189499
!Sample_data_row_count = 0
